{"activity_text": "Antifungal, candidacidal", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Peptide discovery: Octominin II was obtained by deleting the last 5 charged amino acids of Octominin (AP03250). Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (78.26%) to Octominin A: 17%; I=L=N=K: 13%. GRAVY: 0.065; Mol W: 2522.967; Mol formula: C114H196N29O32; Mol Ex coeff: 5550. Activity: active against C. albicans (MIC 80 ug/ml), C. glabrata (MIC 55 ug/ml), and C.auris (MIC 160 ug/ml). In vitro Toxicity: murine RBC, HC50 > 100 ug/ml, ~10% hemo.lytic at 100 ug/ml. Little toxicity to RAW 264.7 cells till 200 ug/ml. However, it showed some toxicity to zebrafish larvae 72 hpf (50% survival after 96 h, n=10) Antivirulence:fungi: it suppressed numreous virulence factors related to drug resistance, genes for the filamentation and hyphal growth, and secreted aspartic proteases; Animal model:Zebrafish: Octominin II decreased the virulence (less nutrophil infiltration) of C. albicans in vivo, which prevents further invasion of Candida.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "37762357", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Int J Mol Sci. 2023 Sep 13;24(18):14053. doi: 10.3390/ijms241814053. Pub-Med.", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03722", "source_id": "AP03722", "source_numeric_id": "03722", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03722", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Antifungal Efficacy of Antimicrobial Peptide Octominin II against Candida albicans", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
